{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XGZ26Jr6gguyD3x6DcAarb","type":"tool_result","content":"schema_version: 1\npatch_id: P-N30-001\naction: overlay\ngraph_id: plan26_langgraph_curriculum_factory_implementation\nbase_graph_digest: b943d0f944251043c34d8fd778043ad25397673df0a7c83b4c791ac2ecf963e8\ntarget_node: N30_UNIT_GRAPH\nscope: node_only\nreason: N31's approved rework (P-N31-001, closing N90 finding F1) necessarily widens\n  the compiled graph's routing, which N30's own frozen test_plan26_unit_graph.py hardcodes\n  assumptions against (binding_inventory()-derived available set, and a clean episode\n  fixture's expected M05->D16 deferred stopping point). Structural, unavoidable consequence,\n  not a defect in unit_graph.py's own logic\nexpected_effect: test_plan26_unit_graph.py derives its expected wired-edge set from\n  the real compiled graph rather than the always-narrow binding_inventory(), and derives\n  the clean-episode fixture's expected halting frontier dynamically rather than hardcoding\n  D16, so it stays correct both before and after D16-D23/D24-D32 are wired\ninstructions: \"Ownership correction, same chain as P-N20-001: N31 has now (per an\\\n  \\ approved\\nimmutable patch, P-N31-001) wired D16-D23/M06 into the one production\\n\\\n  compiled graph, closing N90's finding F1 \\u2014 before this, a real run could\\n\\\n  never reach `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED` for any unit. Six of your own\\ntests\\\n  \\ in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` hardcode assumptions from\\nbefore\\\n  \\ that correction and now fail as a direct, structural consequence \\u2014 not\\n\\\n  because `unit_graph.py`'s own logic (`register_unit_path`, `branch_\\ndestinations`,\\\n  \\ `deferred_destinations`, `DEFERRED_EDGES`, `UNIT_BRANCHES`) is\\nwrong; N31 did\\\n  \\ not touch `unit_graph.py` at all, by design (widening the\\n`available` sequence\\\n  \\ `register_unit_path` receives is what resolves the six\\nN31-owned `DEFERRED_EDGES`\\\n  \\ rows automatically \\u2014 your module's own machinery\\nalready does this correctly\\\n  \\ for whatever `available` it's given).\\n\\nImportant ordering note: at the time\\\n  \\ you run, `runtime/langgraph_factory\\n/graph.py` still only compiles the narrow,\\\n  \\ pre-correction `binding_\\ninventory()` \\u2014 N31's wiring happens in a separate,\\\n  \\ isolated attempt and is\\nmerged in only after your fix here is verified and admitted.\\\n  \\ The six\\nfailures below will not reproduce in your own environment right now.\\\n  \\ Your\\nfix must be correct by construction and verified by your existing suite\\n\\\n  passing cleanly today \\u2014 do not hardcode today's specific behavior anywhere,\\n\\\n  and do not weaken any assertion's actual guarantee, only what it assumes\\nabout\\\n  \\ which nodes are currently wired.\\n\\n- `test_the_compiled_graph_registers_every_declared_unit_branch`\\\n  \\ computes\\n  `expected = branch_destinations(source, available)` from `available\\\n  \\ =\\n  tuple(sorted(binding_inventory()))` (deliberately narrow, per P-N31-001's\\n\\\n  \\  own instruction not to change what `binding_inventory()` returns), then\\n  asserts\\\n  \\ it equals `registered`, read from the real compiled graph's edges.\\n  Once D08/D09/D12/D14/D91's\\\n  \\ guards really do route to D17 (and M05's to\\n  D16) in the real compiled graph,\\\n  \\ `registered` correctly contains those\\n  destinations while `expected` \\u2014\\\n  \\ computed from the frozen narrow\\n  `binding_inventory()` \\u2014 does not, so the\\\n  \\ two can no longer be equal by\\n  construction. Fix this the same way P-N20-001\\\n  \\ fixes the analogous topology\\n  test: derive `available` for this comparison from\\\n  \\ whatever the real\\n  compiled graph's own node set is (`set(compiled.get_graph().nodes)`)\\n\\\n  \\  intersected with what `branch_destinations`/`deferred_destinations`\\n  actually\\\n  \\ need, rather than from `binding_inventory()`'s always-narrow\\n  return value \\u2014\\\n  \\ the test's real job is proving `register_unit_path` wired\\n  exactly the destinations\\\n  \\ that truly have bodies in whatever the production\\n  compile point actually used,\\\n  \\ which is a self-consistency check against the\\n  compiled graph itself, not a\\\n  \\ hardcoded external list frozen at whichever\\n  generation last touched this file.\\n\\\n  - `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`,\\n\\\n  \\  `test_a_visual_denominator_permutation_produces_an_identical_admitted_head`,\\n\\\n  \\  `test_the_committed_path_stops_at_a_declared_deferred_edge`,\\n  `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason`,\\\n  \\ and\\n  `test_this_nodes_renderers_are_a_test_double_and_not_exposed_to_n13s_store_gap`\\n\\\n  \\  all run the shared single-unit `_build_episode_fixture` through\\n  `_run_episode`,\\\n  \\ whose scripted M05 review has no blocking findings. Before\\n  D16 had a real body,\\\n  \\ that episode necessarily dead-ended at the `M05 ->\\n  D16` deferred edge \\u2014\\\n  \\ several of these tests hardcode that specific\\n  frontier (`deferred_frontier\\\n  \\ == \\\"D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE\\\"`, or assertions\\n  that only hold because the\\\n  \\ episode never called `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` a\\n  second time). Now that D16 genuinely\\\n  \\ executes, its denominator legitimately\\n  passes on the first try for this clean\\\n  \\ fixture, so the real run proceeds\\n  through D22/D23, loops back to a second `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`\\\n  \\ call, finds\\n  the one-unit manifest exhausted, and correctly halts on the still-deferred\\n\\\n  \\  `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE` row instead \\u2014 this is the pipeline\\n\\\n  \\  behaving correctly, exactly what N90's finding said was missing, not a\\n  defect\\\n  \\ in this generation's fixture. Do not hardcode the new frontier\\n  (`D24_...`)\\\n  \\ as a literal replacement string either, for the same staleness\\n  reason as above:\\\n  \\ derive \\\"the deferred edge this clean episode currently\\n  halts on\\\" from the\\\n  \\ actual run's own terminal state / `DEFERRED_EDGES`\\n  lookup at test time, so\\\n  \\ this suite keeps working once N32 also closes D24.\\n  If any of these five tests'\\\n  \\ real purpose (not its specific hardcoded\\n  frontier) no longer makes sense once\\\n  \\ D16-D23 execute for real \\u2014 e.g. a\\n  test whose entire point was \\\"prove\\\n  \\ the run stops exactly at the M05->D16\\n  edge\\\" \\u2014 say so explicitly in your\\\n  \\ result report rather than forcing an\\n  artificial fixture (such as injecting\\\n  \\ a blocking M05 finding) purely to\\n  preserve the old stopping point; a real,\\\n  \\ more-complete pipeline run is the\\n  correct outcome here, not a regression to\\\n  \\ route around.\\n\\nDo not touch `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`'s content,\\\n  \\ `repair.py`,\\n`acceptance.py`, or D16-D23's registration logic \\u2014 none of\\\n  \\ that is this\\nnode's concern here; this is a test-fixture correction only, in\\\n  \\ the one file\\nalready in your write set (`tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py`).\\\n  \\ Run\\nyour full existing verification command afterward and confirm it is green.\\n\\\n  Update your own result report to record this correction: cite N90's F1 and\\nP-N31-001\\\n  \\ as the root cause chain, and what changed.\\n\"\ncontext: {}\ncreated_at: '2026-08-12T20:54:45.963329+00:00'","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e29286fb-f991-47f0-8e19-a325c46ee82a","uuid":"c1bcaea3-3d2d-4605-98be-114c17b142d5","timestamp":"2026-08-12T20:58:25.590Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"schema_version: 1\npatch_id: P-N30-001\naction: overlay\ngraph_id: plan26_langgraph_curriculum_factory_implementation\nbase_graph_digest: b943d0f944251043c34d8fd778043ad25397673df0a7c83b4c791ac2ecf963e8\ntarget_node: N30_UNIT_GRAPH\nscope: node_only\nreason: N31's approved rework (P-N31