{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NEQ64X29gFBDMciSTyVa5f","type":"tool_result","content":"278\tdef binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:\n279\t    \"\"\"Every node callable the *skeleton and unit path* resolve against.\n280\t\n281\t    N31's unit-repair-cycle nodes (D16-D23) carry no `NODE_CATALOGUE` row and\n282\t    are absent here: they are exercised at the function level by N31's own\n283\t    tests, and this generation does not wire their topology (spec section\n284\t    8.1's D08/D09/D12/D14/D91 -> D17 and M05 -> D16 edges stay the declared\n285\t    `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows they already are).\n286\t\n287\t    N32's workbook engine (D24-D32, `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`) is\n288\t    likewise absent from *this* function deliberately, not by oversight: D24\n289\t    is `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`'s own `manifest_exhausted` destination, and\n290\t    `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES`/`unit_graph.UNIT_BRANCHES` (N30's frozen,\n291\t    already-verified tables) declare that edge deferred to N32 by name. If D24\n292\t    entered this function, `unit_graph.register_unit_path`'s *own*\n293\t    `available`-derived destination set for `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` would\n294\t    silently widen to include it -- correct for a production run, but it\n295\t    would falsify N30's own already-passing topology tests, which independently\n296\t    recompute their expectation from this exact function's return value.\n297\t    `register_workbook_topology` registers the workbook engine as an additive\n298\t    step over its own separate builder (N32 exercises it directly, not through\n299\t    `build_curriculum_factory_graph`), so the unit path's registered edges stay\n300\t    byte-identical to what they were before N32 and the workbook branch is\n301\t    still fully real -- just not reachable from `D05` in this generation,\n302\t    exactly as `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` documents.\n303\t    \"\"\"\n304\t\n305\t    bindings: dict[str, Callable[..., Any]] = dict(node_registry())\n306\t    for job_id, adapter in MODEL_NODE_ADAPTERS.items():\n307\t        bindings[job_id] = adapter\n308\t    bindings.update(MODEL_BOOKKEEPING_NODES)\n309\t    return bindings\n310\t\n311\t\n312\tdef full_binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:\n313\t    \"\"\"`binding_inventory()` plus N32's workbook engine (D24-D32).\n314\t\n315\t    The complete node set the compiled graph actually registers. Kept\n316\t    separate from `binding_inventory()` itself for the reason documented\n317\t    there: several of N30's own tests recompute their expectation directly\n318\t    from `binding_inventory()`'s return value, so that function's contract\n319\t    (the skeleton/unit-path view) must stay exactly what it was before N32.\n320\t    \"\"\"\n321\t\n322\t    bindings = dict(binding_inventory())\n323\t    bindings.update(workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES)\n324\t    return bindings\n325\t\n326\t\n327\tdef _reject(code: str, node_id: str, detail: str) -> None:\n328\t    raise GraphBindingError(f\"{code}:{node_id}: {detail}\")\n329\t\n330\t\n331\tdef validate_bindings(\n332\t    bindings: Mapping[str, Callable[..., Any]],\n333\t    *,\n334\t    required: Sequence[str],\n335\t) -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:\n336\t    \"\"\"Reject a missing, placeholder, test-only, duplicate, or unusable binding.\"\"\"\n337\t\n338\t    for node_id in required:\n339\t        if node_id not in bindings:\n340\t            _reject(\"N20-BIND-MISSING\", node_id, \"no production callable is registered\")\n341\t\n342\t    seen: dict[tuple[str, str], str] = {}\n343\t    inventory: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n344\t    for node_id in sorted(bindings):\n345\t        body = bindings[node_id]\n346\t        if not callable(body):\n347\t            _reject(\"N20-BIND-UNCALLABLE\", node_id, f\"binding is {type(body).__name__}\")"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e29286fb-f991-47f0-8e19-a325c46ee82a","uuid":"043c6cb7-3125-4a37-b3f5-972c3f900914","timestamp":"2026-08-12T21:02:35.247Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/attempt-20260812T205813.582887Z-e473c586b2/repo/runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py","content":"def binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every node callable the *skeleton and unit path* resolve against.\n\n    N31's unit-repair-cycle nodes (D16-D23) carry no `NODE_CATALOGUE` row and\n    are absent here: they are exercised at the function level by N31's own\n    tests, and this generation does not wire their topology (spec section\n    8.1's D08/D09/D12/D14/D91 -> D17 and M05 -> D16 edges stay the declared\n    `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows they already are).\n\n    N32's workbook engine (D24-D32, `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`) is\n    likewise absent from *this* function deliberately, not by oversight: D24\n    is `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`'s own `manifest_exhausted` destination, and\n    `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES`/`unit_graph.UNIT_BRANCHES` (N30's frozen,\n    already-verified tables) declare that edge deferred to N32 by name. If D24\n    entered this function, `unit_graph.register_unit_path`'s *own*\n    `available`-derived destination set for `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` would\n    silently widen to include it -- correct for a production run, but it\n    would falsify N30's own already-passing topology tests, which independently\n    recompute their expectation from this exact function's return value.\n    `register_workbook_topology` registers the workbook engine as an additive\n    step over its own separate builder (N32 exercises it directly, not through\n    `build_curriculum_factory_graph`), so the unit path's registered edges stay\n    byte-identical to what they were before N32 and the workbook branch is\n    still fully real -- just not reachable from `D05` in this generation,\n    exactly as `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` documents.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    bindings: dict[str, Callable[..., Any]] = dict(node_registry())\n    for job_id, adapter in MODEL_NODE_ADAPTERS.items():\n        bindings[job_id] = adapter\n    bindings.update(MODEL_BOOKKEEPING_NODES)\n    return bindings\n\n\ndef full_binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:\n    \"\"\"`binding_inventory()` plus N32's workbook engine (D24-D32).\n\n    The complete node set the compiled graph actually registers. Kept\n    separate from `binding_inventory()` itself for the reason documented\n    there: several of N30's own tests recompute their expectation directly\n    from `binding_inventory()`'s return value, so that function's contract\n    (the skeleton/unit-path view) must stay exactly what it was before N32.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    bindings = dict(binding_inventory())\n    bindings.update(workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES)\n    return bindings\n\n\ndef _reject(code: str, node_id: str, detail: str) -> None:\n    raise GraphBindingError(f\"{code}:{node_id}: {detail}\")\n\n\ndef validate_bindings(\n    bindings: Mapping[str, Callable[..., Any]],\n    *,\n    required: Sequence[str],\n) -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Reject a missing, placeholder, test-only, duplicate, or unusable binding.\"\"\"\n\n    for node_id in required:\n        if node_id not in bindings:\n            _reject(\"N20-BIND-MISSING\", node_id, \"no production callable is registered\")\n\n    seen: dict[tuple[str, str], str] = {}\n    inventory: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    for node_id in sorted(bindings):\n        body = bindings[node_id]\n        if not callable(body):\n            _reject(\"N20-BIND-UNCALLABLE\", node_id, f\"binding is {type(body).__name__}\")","numLines":70,"startLine":278,"totalLines":573}}}
