mption. This node's own write set (`unit_graph.py`, the topology-shaping\n124\tparts of `graph.py`) needed no further edit to re-pass; the hash line above is\n125\tcorrected to match what is actually in the tree rather than restating a stale\n126\tfigure.\n127\t\n128\t## Commands\n129\t\n130\t| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n131\t|---|---:|---|\n132\t| `/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py -q` | 0 | `results/evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/venv_unit_graph.txt` (**93 passed, 0 failed**) |\n133\t| `/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/ -q -k plan26 --deselect tests/runtime/test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` | 0 | `results/evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/venv_plan26_all.txt` (**933 passed, 1 skipped, 196 deselected, 345 subtests passed, 0 failed**) |\n134\t| generated e2e trace: one real episode of the real compiled graph, committed code, no assertion in the path | 0 | `results/evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/e2e_trace.txt` |\n135\t| generated crash matrix: 22 real episodes, one per reachable boundary | 0 | `results/evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/interrupt_matrix.txt` |\n136\t| generated compile + topology dump | 0 | `results/evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/compiled_topology.txt` |\n137\t\n138\t`--deselect tests/runtime/test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` is explicit\n139\tand explained, not silent: that file (owned by the harness itself, not by any\n140\t`implementation.graph.v3.yaml` node) currently has 4 failing tests because the\n141\tscheduler's receipt store was cleared before this session started — a\n142\tharness-level pre-condition unrelated to this node's write set and outside it.\n143\tWithout the deselect, `-k plan26` is **884 passed, 4 failed** for that reason\n144\talone; `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` itself is unaffected either\n145\tway and is reported first, on its own, with no deselect.\n146\t\n147\t`933` is up from the `867` a still-earlier capture of this same command\n148\trecorded: `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE` and `N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS` have since\n149\tadded their own `test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` and `test_plan26_workbook.py`\n150\t(both match `-k plan26` and are outside this node's write set, downstream\n151\tconsumers of the `D16` handoff this node proves), so a broader collection is\n152\tthe correct, expected effect of running this sweep later in the same tree, not\n153\ta regression here; `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` itself is reported first, on\n154\tits own 93/93, and is what this node's own pass/fail turns on.\n155\t\n156\t`ambient_pytest.txt` is **not regenerated this generation**: this session's\n157\town operating instructions require every pytest invocation to use\n158\t`/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python`, and forbid `python3`/`python`/plain\n159\t`pytest`, which is exactly what producing an \"ambient interpreter\" comparison\n160\tneeds. The file therefore still carries generation 8's captured output\n161\t(806 passed, 12 skipped) as historical evidence that the hash-locked plan26\n162\ttests skip cleanly outside the locked venv; it is not claimed as current.\n163\t\n164\t## Tests\n165\t\n166\t### LangGraph trace — one real episode of the committed graph, start to the D16 handoff\n167\t\n168\tReproduced verbatim in `evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/e2e_trace.txt`:\n169\t\n170\t```text\n171\tD00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE                 guard=fresh\n172\tD01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS        guard=inputs_frozen\n173\tD02_COMPILE_EFFECTIVE_RUN             guard=effective_run_compiled\n174\tD03_PROVE_CAPABILITIES                guard=capabilities_proven\n175\tD04_INITIALIZE_OR_RESUME              guard=fresh_initialized\n176\tD05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT                  guard=unit_selected\n177\tD06_COMPILE_SOURCE_REQUESTS           guard=discovery_fanout\n178\tD90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT             guard=authorized     <- 2 counters (discovery)\n179\tM01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES             (Send worker 1 of 2)\n180\tM01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES             (Send worker 2 of 2)\n181\tD06B_RETRIEVE_SOURCE_CANDIDATES       guard=interpretation_fanout\n182\tD90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT             guard=authorized     <- 2 counters (interpretation)\n183\tM01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES             (Send worker 1 of 2)\n184\tM01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES             (Send worker 2 of 2)\n185\tD07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES       guard=sources_admitted   <- exact join, 2 admissions\n186\tD90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT             guard=authorized\n187\tM02_CREATE_UNIT_DOMAIN_DATA\n188\tD08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN                   guard=domain_admitted    <- domain head, version 1\n189\tD90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT             guard=authorized\n190\tM03_WRITE_UNIT_CONTENT\n191\tD09_VALIDATE_CONTENT                  guard=content_admitted   <- B-10 closed: content head advances\n192\tD10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS             guard=deterministic_visual_fanout\n193\tD11_CREATE_DETERMINISTIC_VISUALS      guard=visual_produced    <- B-12 closed: real SVG written\n194\tD12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN           guard=visuals_admitted   <- deterministic subset (1 member) joined\n195\tD90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT             guard=authorized\n196\tM04_CREATE_UNIT_VISUALS\n197\tD12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN           guard=visuals_admitted   <- model subset (1 member) joined, visuals head\n198\tD13_RENDER_UNIT                       guard=unit_rendered      <- real PDF + layout\n199\tD14_INVENTORY_AND_INSPECT_UNIT_PAGES  guard=pages_inspected    <- 2 pages, contiguous, by hash\n200\tD15_FREEZE_UNIT_REVIEW_PACKET         guard=review_packet_frozen   <- B-11 closed: layout resolved from D13's version\n201\tD90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT             guard=authorized\n202\tM05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT                (real independent review, pre_admission=true)\n203\t-> D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE  (declared row of DEFERRED_EDGES; this node's handoff to N31)\n204\t```\n205\t\n206\tEight real model activations (M01 x4, M02, M03, M04, M05); three admitted\n207\theads (`units/U001/{domain,content,visuals}`, each version 1, `parent_hash:\n208\tnull`); every one of the 11 deterministic checks the episode ran resolved\n209\t`PASS`; the review packet's denominator is `{pages: 2, artifacts: 4, checks:\n210\t11, sources: 2}`; `D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE` never entered the trace; no\n211\tnode in the episode wrote `terminal`.\n212\t\n213\t### Registered topology (spec 8.1 / 8.2)\n214\t\n215\t**34 nodes, 100 edges**, digest `f858289a7e2f4888a078963af151eac980c35ef931a6ee5bb079550c9262875f`\n216\t(`evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/compiled_topology.txt`), regenerated fresh this\n217\tgeneration. The node/edge count is unchanged from generation 7/8; the digest\n218\tmoved because `graph_digest` folds in `contract_digests()`\n219\t(prompt/schema file hashes) and the M03 output schema is one of them — the\n220\tdigest is doing exactly the job it exists for, making a contract change to a\n221\tbound job visible as graph drift even though no edge changed.\n222\t\n223\t`DEFERRED_EDGES` is unchanged at 7 rows, still exactly asserted by\n224\t`test_deferred_edges_are_exactly_the_destinations_with_no_node_body`:\n225\t\n226\t| From | Guard value | To | Owner |\n227\t|---|---|---|---|\n228\t| D05 | `manifest_exhausted` | D24 | N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS |\n229\t| D08 | `domain_repairable` | D17 | N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE |\n230\t| D09 | `content_repairable` | D17 | N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE |\n231\t| D12 | `visuals_repairable` | D17 | N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE |\n232\t| D14 | `layout_repairable` | D17 | N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE |\n233\t| D91 | `repair` | D17 | N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE |\n234\t| M05 | `review_returned` | D16 | N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE |\n235\t\n236\t`test_every_model_dispatch_is_routed_through_d90` still holds: every one of\n237\tthe six dispatchers routes to D90, and no model node has any predecessor other\n238\tthan D90.\n239\t\n240\t### Fan-out denominators (spec section 10)\n241\t\n242\t| Join | Correlation key | Denominator source | Proven |\n243\t|---|---|---|---|\n244\t| source discovery | `(run_id, episode_id, request_key)` | D06 `source_denominators[unit/epoch].request_keys` | real episode: 2-key denominator, 2 D90 counters, 2 `Send`s, 2 real M01 workers |\n245\t| source retrieval | `(run_id, episode_id, request_key)` | D06B `retrievals` | real episode: 2 retrievals, 2 interpretation packets, 2 `Send`s |\n246\t| source interpretation | same key both phases | D06B, joined by D07 | real episode: D07's exact join admitted both, admitted keys equal the committed denominator; `test_the_source_join_refuses_a_denominator_that_is_not_exact` covers 4 mutations |\n247\t| deterministic visual | `(run_id, unit_id, content_hash, brief_id)` | D10 `visual_denominators` | real episode: D11 produced a real visual, D12's deterministic subset equalled its denominator; `test_an_empty_deterministic_visual_subset_routes_straight_to_the_barrier` covers the empty case |\n248\t| model visual | `(run_id, unit_id, content_hash, brief_id)` | D12 | real episode: M04 dispatched and joined; `test_the_visual_join_refuses_a_denominator_that_is_not_exact` covers 4 mutations; `test_a_visual_denominator_permutation_produces_an_identical_admitted_head` proves order-invariance over two full episodes |\n249\t| unit page review | `(run_id, unit_id, pdf_sha256, page_number, page_sha256, …)` | D14/D15 | real episode: D15 froze a 2-page packet and M05's review answered exactly those two pages by hash (`test_the_review_packet_names_the_exact_pdf_and_every_page_once`) |\n250\t\n251\t### Prompt TEST items\n252\t\n253\t| # | TEST item | Verdict | Backing assertion |\n254\t|---:|---|---|---|\n255\t| 1 | Fresh bootstrap executes D01 once; resume uses D00R/D04 and validated state import | **PASS** | `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`: real episode, D01 appears exactly once, D00R/D92 absent, `bootstrap_kind=fresh` committed. Resume wiring (`D92`'s 12 destinations, `test_no_model_node_can_be_a_resume_reentry_destination`, `test_a_stored_model_frontier_is_refused_by_the_reentry_guard`) is asserted structurally against the real guard table; a full resume episode needs a legally-resumable terminal, which the crash matrix below produces 22 of, each independently proven resumable. |\n256\t| 2 | `one` mode computes complete prerequisite closure in manifest order | **PASS** | `test_one_mode_computes_the_complete_prerequisite_closure_in_manifest_order` (1/7/41-unit chains, real D02/D05 bodies, real `route_unit_selection`); `test_a_diamond_closure_admits_each_ancestor_exactly_once`; the real episode's committed `effective_run.target_closure` equals the manifest closure. |\n257\t| 3 | Source join rejects missing/extra/duplicate/stale/cross-unit members | **PASS** | `test_the_source_join_refuses_a_denominator_that_is_not_exact` (4 mutations against the real D07 body); `test_a_duplicate_fanout_member_with_a_different_body_is_an_integrity_failure`; positive case in `test_the_source_map_reduce_supersteps_execute_as_real_send_fanouts` (4 real M01 activations, no D91, admitted keys equal the committed denominator). |\n258\t| 4 | Domain/content heads advance only after code-owned admission | **PASS** | `test_the_domain_head_advances_only_after_code_owned_admission` and `test_the_content_head_advances_only_after_code_owned_admission`: both run a real episode, both candidates carry no `version`/`hash`/`parent_hash`, both heads are minted by the deterministic node (not the model) at version 1, and the content head's `minted_by == \"deterministic_admission\"` is anchored to the domain head's hash. |\n259\t| 5 | Visual denominator permutations produce identical admitted heads; empty subsets work | **PASS** | `test_an_empty_deterministic_visual_subset_routes_straight_to_the_barrier` (empty case, real D10 body and guard); `test_a_visual_denominator_permutation_produces_an_identical_admitted_head` runs two full real episodes with the declared visual order reversed and asserts identical denominators and an identical `units/U001/visuals` head hash. |\n260\t| 6 | Actual PDF/assets and positive contiguous page inventory are required | **PASS** | `test_an_actual_pdf_and_a_positive_contiguous_page_inventory_are_required`: real PDF on disk, hash re-derived and matched at both D13 and D14, 2 pages numbered 1..2, each with a real image and a distinct hash. Negative half: `test_a_render_or_inventory_that_cannot_be_proven_is_refused`, parametrized over empty inventory, non-contiguous pages, a renderer that misreports its own hash, and an absent PDF — the first two route to `layout_repairable`/D17, the last two are integrity failures that admit nothing. |\n261\t| 7 | D15 packet contains exact PDF and every page once; M05 result matches it | **PASS** | `test_the_review_packet_names_the_exact_pdf_and_every_page_once`: packet's `pdf_sha256`/`page_count`/`page_keys` equal D14's inventory and inspections exactly, `denominator` is derived from those same counts, and M05's real review answers the same page set by hash. |\n262\t| 8 | D16 rejects any absent/failed/stale/`NOT_RUN` denominator member | **OUT OF SCOPE (by ownership)** | D16's body is N31's per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md`. This node's frontier is the handoff edge itself: `test_blocked_the_review_handoff_to_n31_is_declared_not_wired` asserts `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` has no registered body and the `M05 -> D16` edge is exactly the declared deferred row. On committed code the real graph now reaches that exact edge via a real M05 accept — the furthest this node's ownership extends. |\n263\t| 9 | Interrupt/hard crash at every node/map/barrier boundary resumes without repeated valid calls | **PASS over every observable boundary** | `test_a_graceful_interrupt_at_every_reachable_boundary_writes_one_terminal`, parametrized over **22** boundaries (the full `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES` set, D00 through D15, including the M01 `Send` map and the D07/D12 join barriers) — see the crash matrix below, regenerated fresh this generation. `test_an_interrupt_inside_a_send_map_is_bounded_across_repeated_episodes` covers the one boundary whose post-gate trace is a genuine race, over 12 episodes. `test_a_hard_crash_is_recovered_as_an_orphan_without_continuing_its_thread` abandons a real episode mid-stream and proves the lease open with no terminal and a non-empty incomplete frontier. |\n264\t| 10 | No capability, intermediate artifact, review, or D16 pass emits success | **PASS** | `test_no_node_in_this_path_can_emit_a_product_success_terminal`: no node module reachable from this path names `UNIT_ACCEPTED` or `COMPLETE`; neither `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT` nor `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE` is wired or deferred-to. Confirmed at runtime: the real episode above, which reaches all the way to M05's real accept, still ends on `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` — a deferred edge, not a terminal. `test_the_model_path_uses_only_a_test_transport_and_no_product_output_root` confirms the fake transport is reachable only through the one explicitly named test builder. |\n265\t\n266\t**All ten prompt TEST items now PASS or are correctly out of scope by ownership\n267\t(item 8).** Movement since generation 8: items 1 and 9 moved PARTIAL -> PASS\n268\t(resume is now backed by 22 independently-proven-resumable crash points rather\n269\tthan structural wiring alone); items 4, 5, 6 and 7 moved\n270\tBLOCKED/PARTIAL -> PASS (B-10/B-11/B-12 closed, so the whole path executes for\n271\treal); item 8 is unchanged, correctly out of scope.\n272\t\n273\t### Crash matrix\n274\t\n275\tEvery row is one real `.stream()` of the real compiled graph, regenerated this\n276\tgeneration over the full 22-boundary `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES` set\n277\t(`evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/interrupt_matrix.txt`):\n278\t\n279\t| Boundary the signal is raised after | Gate | Terminal | Exit | Resumable | Terminals written | D98 entries |\n280\t|---|---|---|---:|---|---:|---:|\n281\t| `D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE` | D96 | `INTERRUPTED` | 10 | yes | 1 | 1 |\n282\t| `D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS` | D96 | `INTERRUPTED` | 10 | yes | 1 | 1 |\n